(:include "tiers/feed.domain")
(:include "tiers/idle.domain")

// Mouse: eat when hungry or thirsty, else idle. The smallest creature root: two branches, each delegating to a
// shared tier.
//
// Teaches: a short root that delegates, shared tiers by `:include`, and a GUARD ON EVERY ROOT BRANCH.
// The source's root branches have no conditions: SS14 relies on `FoodCompound` failing (no hunger, no food) and the
// planner falling through to `IdleCompound`. Our default mode (ALL) would fall through too, but with branch
// backtracking off (FACTS_AND_AXIOMS, NONE) the selected branch commits and there is no plan.
// So the port states each tier's real precondition on its root branch (`#feed_target`): the root reads as a priority
// list with reasons, the debugger shows why a tier was skipped instead of a failed subtree, it costs no failed
// decomposition, and the plan is the same with or without branch backtracking (test/examples/canon/canon.test.ts checks
// ALL against FACTS_AND_AXIOMS for every scenario).
// Source: Space Station 14 (MIT), `MouseCompound` in Resources/Prototypes/NPCs/mob.yml at commit
// 614f030530578e248a2393dd71ee9813d68d800d:
// https://github.com/space-wizards/space-station-14/blob/614f030530578e248a2393dd71ee9813d68d800d/Resources/Prototypes/NPCs/mob.yml
// Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2017-2026 Space Wizards Federation; see src/examples/canon/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
// Adapted (YAML prototypes re-written in our domain language).
// Deviations: the guard (above); the target travels from the guard into the tier as a parameter.
// Not ported: the rest of mob.yml's roots (cockroach-likes, the mop roach's puddle tier, ranged roaches): same
// shape, other tiers.
//
// Facts and primitives: see tiers/feed.domain and tiers/idle.domain.

(:domain Mouse top_level_domain

    (:method (behave) top_level_method

        (eat
            (and
                (#feed_target ?item)
            )
            (
                (feed ?item)
            )
        )

        (idle
            ()
            (
                (idle)
            )
        )
    )
)
